=== REASONING ===
Phase 38's earlier prompts (01-06) shifted the live-store boundary from "drop unknown freshness / drop stale" to "return everything; freshness is per-value via IsLiveSignalFresh", added a signal_log SnapshotAt fallback in BuildStateFromSignalStore, and added a Warm-time legacy scalar restamp in HybridLiveSignalStore.Warm. The docs and ADR still describe the OLD silent-drop policy ("treat... as stale and legacy scalar Redis values as unknown freshness" implied dropping them at the boundary), which is now wrong. ADR-007 must be updated so future agents do not "fix" the new code by re-introducing the silent drops.

Source-of-truth anchors used to verify each new doc claim against code:
  - Merge rule (newer wins, ties prefer L2, both-zero L1): mergeSignalValues at internal/signal/live_store.go:347-379. mergeSignalMaps at lines 384-403 confirms the GetAll path returns the union of L1 and L2 keys with the merge rule per signal.
  - "Freshness informational, not a filter": GetSignal/GetAll docstrings at internal/signal/live_store.go:169-226 ("Stale and legacy zero-Timestamp L2 values are retained ... the read path does not drop them"). Test coverage: TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAllReturnsStaleL2EnvelopesWithTimestampPreserved (live_store_test.go:770-806), TestHybridLiveSignalStoreGetAllMergesL1AndL2WithNewerTimestampWinning (live_store_test.go:808+).
  - signal_log SnapshotAt(now) fallback: BuildStateFromSignalStore at internal/service/vehicle_service.go:264-277 ("Phase 2: signal_log fallback for fields the live store left at their Go zero value ... reading from snapshot tables ... is forbidden. Live values always win — the fallback only fills holes.").
  - Warm-time restamp: HybridLiveSignalStore.Warm at internal/signal/live_store.go:228-254, RedisSignalCache.RestampLegacy in internal/signal/redis_cache.go (per phase-38-06 log: "RestampLegacy decodes via decodeLegacySignalValue then re-encodes via encodeTimestampedSignalValue ... idempotent ... TTL refreshed via Expire").

